=3D"ato-Businessesinthisindustry"><a id=3D"Whoisinthisindustry" class=3D"an=
chor"></a>Businesses in this industry</h2>
<p>Businesses in this industry install, repair and maintain:</p>
<ul>
    <li>ventilation</li>
    <li>air conditioning</li>
    <li>heating</li>
    <li>refrigeration systems.</li>
</ul>
<p>They may also install ducting and construct freezers and cool rooms.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ato-Whatareperformancebenchmarks"><a id=3D"Whatareperformancebenc=
hmarks10" class=3D"anchor"></a>What are performance benchmarks</h2>
<p>Performance benchmarks use information reported on tax returns for the 2=
023=E2=80=9324&nbsp;financial year and are updated each year. This is the m=
ost current data.</p>
<p>The benchmarks show ranges of business income to business expenses. Use =
these benchmarks to <a href=3D"https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organi=
sations/income-deductions-and-concessions/small-business-benchmarks/compare=
-your-business-now">compare your performance</a> against similar businesses=
.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ato-Keybenchmarkrange"><a id=3D"Keybenchmarkrange11" class=3D"anc=
hor"></a>Key benchmark range</h2>
<p>Total expenses to turnover is the key benchmark range for this industry.=
 It is the most accurate when predicting business turnover.</p>
<p>You should fall within the key benchmark range for your annual turnover.=
 If you fall outside the range, there may be room for your business to impr=
ove.</p>
<p>Check you reported all income and accounted for any trading stock you <a=
 href=3D"https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organisations/income-deducti=
ons-and-concessions/income-and-deductions-for-business/accounting-for-tradi=
ng-stock/using-stock-for-private-purposes">used for private purposes</a>. S=
ome businesses can use accepted amounts as estimates for the value of tradi=
ng stock used for private purposes.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ato-202324benchmarks"><a id=3D"BK_202122benchmarks" class=3D"anch=
or"></a>2023=E2=80=9324 benchmarks</h2>
<table>
    <caption>Key benchmarks for 2023=E2=80=9324</caption>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <th>
            <p>Annual turnover range</p>
            </th>
            <th class=3D"alignRight">
            <p>$50,000 =E2=80=93 $150,000</p>
            </th>
            <th class=3D"alignRight">
            <p>$150,001 =E2=80=93 $600,000</p>
            </th>
            <th class=3D"alignRight">
            <p>More than $600,000</p>
            </th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th>
            <p>'Total expenses' divided by 'Annual turnover'</p>
            </th>
            <td>
            <p class=3D"alignRight">54%&nbsp;to&nbsp;73%</p>
            </td>
            <td>
            <p class=3D"alignRight">65%&nbsp;to&nbsp;78%</p>
            </td>
            <td>
            <p class=3D"alignRight">79%&nbsp;to&nbsp;89%</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th>
            <p>Average total expenses</p>
            </th>
            <td>
            <p class=3D"alignRight">63%</p>
            </td>
            <td>
            <p class=3D"alignRight">72%</p>
            </td>
            <td>
            <p class=3D"alignRight">84%</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
